---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---
<Base title="CV" description="CV of Nihal Sulaiman: data analyst and BI developer, Master's in Data Analytics, MSc Physics. Python, SQL, star schemas, dashboards, forecasting and machine learning.">
  <section class="phero"><div class="in cv cv-head">
    <div>
      <p class="crumbs no-print"><a href="/">Home</a> / CV</p>
      <h1>Nihal Vellaramkallingal Sulaiman</h1>
      <p class="lead">Data analyst and BI developer · Niagara Falls, Ontario · open to anywhere in Ontario</p>
      <div class="btns no-print"><button class="btn primary" type="button" onclick="window.print()">Print or save as PDF</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="contact">
      <a href={SITE.links.linkedin}>linkedin.com/in/vsnihal</a>
      <a href={SITE.links.github}>github.com/nihalunfc</a>
      <a href={SITE.links.kaggle}>kaggle.com/vsnihal</a>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <main class="cv">
    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <p>Data analyst and BI developer with a Master's in Data Analytics and an MSc in Physics (astrophysics). I build end-to-end data work in Python and SQL, from pipelines and star-schema warehouses to dashboards, forecasts and machine-learning models, and I test every result on data it hasn't seen. Hotel operations experience from the floor, and top-10% Kaggle results.</p>

    <h2>Projects</h2>
    <ol class="tl">
      <li><span class="when">2026</span><div><h3><a href="/projects/hospitality-bi/">Hospitality BI for a five-hotel group</a></h3><ul>
        <li>Built a star-schema warehouse of about 640,000 synthetic bookings over four years, with ten automated data-quality checks and unit tests.</li>
        <li>Built a revenue command centre (occupancy, ADR, RevPAR, pace, back-tested demand forecast) and a staff schedule builder that turns forecast workload into shifts with PuLP and checks Ontario labour rules.</li>
      </ul></div></li>
      <li><span class="when">2026</span><div><h3><a href="/projects/swarm-intelligence/">Swarm Intelligence</a> and <a href="/projects/warl-wildfire/">WARL wildfire drones</a></h3><ul>
        <li>Multi-agent reinforcement learning (PyTorch DQN) for grid batteries, wildfire drones and hotel operations, compared against today's operating rules.</li>
        <li>Live dashboards in JavaScript, D3 and Leaflet, with a Gemini-powered explainable-AI chatbot.</li>
      </ul></div></li>
      <li><span class="when">2026</span><div><h3><a href="/kaggle/">Kaggle competitions</a></h3><ul>
        <li>Name That LLM: 436th of 4,346 teams (top 10%) attributing passages to 18 LLMs; built prompt-grouped, leak-free validation for LoRA-tuned Qwen and Llama ensembles.</li>
        <li>Enveda CASMI 2026: built a leak-free 300-structure hold-out that predicted leaderboard drops the provided validation panel missed.</li>
        <li>Mallorn Challenge: top 15% with gradient-boosted models.</li>
      </ul></div></li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Experience</h2>
    <ol class="tl">
      <li><span class="when">Current</span><div><h3>AI Training Specialist (remote)</h3><div class="where">Shipd by DataCurve</div></div></li>
      <li><span class="when">Over a year</span><div><h3>Room Attendant</h3><div class="where">Hotel housekeeping, Niagara Falls, Ontario</div><ul><li>Also trained as Night Maid and Houseman.</li></ul></div></li>
      <li><span class="when">2019 to 2022</span><div><h3>Founder, ad-supported content websites</h3><div class="where">Self-employed, India</div><ul><li>Managed content, traffic, ad revenue and marketing data.</li></ul></div></li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Education</h2>
    <ol class="tl">
      <li><span class="when">2026</span><div><h3>Master's in Data Analytics</h3><div class="where">University of Niagara Falls Canada</div></div></li>
      <li><span class="when">2017 to 2019</span><div><h3>MSc Physics (astrophysics major, mathematics minor)</h3><div class="where">Cochin University of Science and Technology, India</div></div></li>
      <li><span class="when">2013 to 2016</span><div><h3>BSc Physics</h3><div class="where">Government Victoria College, University of Calicut, India</div></div></li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Skills</h2>
    <dl class="skills">
      <dt>Data and BI</dt><dd>Python (pandas, NumPy, Polars), SQL (SQL Server, SQLite), dimensional modelling, data-quality testing, Excel; learning Power BI and DAX</dd>
      <dt>Modelling</dt><dd>Forecasting, optimisation (PuLP), XGBoost, LightGBM, CatBoost, Optuna, scikit-learn</dd>
      <dt>Deep learning and AI</dt><dd>PyTorch, Hugging Face Transformers, LoRA fine-tuning, reinforcement learning, Gemini API</dd>
      <dt>Web and tools</dt><dd>JavaScript, D3, Leaflet, HTML and CSS, Git and GitHub, Databricks, Google Cloud, LaTeX, Claude Code</dd>
    </dl>
  </main>
</Base>
